    "turn_text": "Well, part of the problem when you have your institutions that historically have been respected, when they are obliterated, people lose their confidence, and these institutions that were put in place for explicitly good purpose. They evolve, they all evolve, but this is a problem. The presidency's lost its legitimacy in many ways, Congress has lost its legitimacy in many ways. The Supreme Court has lost its legitimacy in many, many ways. The Catholic Church, I mean, you just keep going on and on. The elections, look what's going on with elections. The principles that were established in 1965, Voting Rights Act, you can be criminally charged for giving a woman who's standing in line to vote in Georgia about all water. This is bad, bad stuff, and I do believe that the vast majority of Americans are of good purpose. But the radicalization of this, this, this, you know, Trump faction of Americans is, you know, the good thing is buying got more votes than any president in the history of American presidents. Trump got second. highest votes. So the interesting thing is Trump never received majority of the popular vote. So the irony is that he got the exact number of 306 electoral votes in beating Hillary Clinton that Biden got. and this past election beating him and he won Biden won seven million more of the popular vote and somehow his election was stolen.",
